From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MobOpt Paper <mobopt@localhost>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 05:10:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Optimize Paper network framing and dispatch

Keep Paper's packet FIFO, protocol transitions, promises, and listener
semantics intact while removing avoidable transport overhead. Complete inbound
frames and compression pass-through payloads can use retained slices. Outbound
encoders reserve safe frame-prefix headroom and retain the original fallback
for shared, sliced, composite, read-only, or third-party buffers.

During Paper's server-thread flush suspension, PLAY writes use Netty's normal
FIFO task queue without waking the selector for every packet; the existing
normal end-of-tick flush supplies the wakeup. Pending, async, immediate-flush,
and non-PLAY writes keep normal scheduling. Queued packet actions also avoid a
per-entry AtomicBoolean and capturing delegate allocation.

Explosion recipients are selected from Moonrise's maintained wide nearby-player
index before the original strict three-dimensional 64-block check. Section
block updates, packet construction, compression, encryption, and plugin-visible
packet objects are unchanged.

